Body:
@rekram1-node  No, no plugins at all. This was actually my first time trying OpenCode.
The only thing I configured (the project is fairly heavy) was sub-agents :)
However, the amount of work they managed to get done was several times less than what a single Codex CLI does..

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "experimental": {
    "mcp_timeout": 600000
  }
}
```

This worked for me in addressing the unexpectedly-short ("McpError: MCP error -32001: Request timed out") timeout issue. (I set my timeout here to 10 minutes)

If I understand correctly, this is configurable via your `opencode.json` config with these parameters:

```json
{
  provider: {
    customprovider: {
      name: My Custom Provider,
      npm: @ai-sdk/openai-compatible,
      options: {
        apiKey: {env:API_KEY},
        baseURL: https://api.example.com
      },
      models: {
        my-model-name: {
          limit: { context: 1000000, output: 32000 },
          cost: { input: 0.3, output: 1.2 },
          temperature: true,
          reasoning: true,
          tool_call: true
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
